# Attribution Service -- deployment configuration.
#
# The container image carries no deployment-specific values, so this file is
# required rather than optional. Install it at the path the service reads at
# startup, and no run-command argument is needed:
#
#   cp attrsvc.env.example /var/lib/nvrx/attrsvc.env   # then edit
#
# /var/lib/nvrx rather than /var/log/nvrx: this is state, not a log, and
# attrsvc already keeps its cache there. Deployments mount that directory
# read-write already, so the file needs no mount of its own.
#
# --env-file and -e still work and take precedence, so a deployment that
# already passes configuration explicitly keeps doing so. Point the service
# elsewhere with NVRX_ATTRSVC_ENV_FILE, or set it empty to ignore the file.
# This is read by the service itself, so it applies to the systemd, SLURM
# and container deployments alike, not only to docker run.
#
# The same variables are what the systemd unit reads from
# /etc/nvrx/nvrx.env via EnvironmentFile, so a host can share one file.
#
# docker --env-file does not do shell quoting: write VALUE, not "VALUE".

# -- Bind address ------------------------------------------------------------
# The container image already sets both, because binding all interfaces is what
# running in a namespace requires rather than a site preference. Set them here
# only for a host install, where the service's own 127.0.0.1 default applies,
# or to move the container off port 8000.
# NVRX_ATTRSVC_HOST=0.0.0.0
# NVRX_ATTRSVC_PORT=8000

# -- Log access --------------------------------------------------------------
# Every path the service is allowed to read logs from must sit under this root.
NVRX_ATTRSVC_ALLOWED_ROOT=/data/logs

# -- Model credentials -------------------------------------------------------
# A file, so the key is not visible in the container environment or in
# "docker inspect". Mount it read-only.
LLM_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/llm_api_key

# -- Service logging ---------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. stderr always works and the container runtime keeps it on the host;
# this writes a second copy somewhere a shared filesystem can see, which is how
# startup problems get diagnosed without shell access to the node. Rotated at
# 64 MB with 3 backups kept, so it cannot fill the mount. Leave unset to stay
# on stderr only.
NVRX_ATTRSVC_LOG_FILE=/var/log/nvrx/attrsvc.log
NVRX_ATTRSVC_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# -- Alerting ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated channel ids. Unset disables Slack alerting entirely.
# These two are read without the NVRX_ATTRSVC_ prefix the other settings
# use, so that a host already holding a Slack token can share it.
# SLACK_CHANNEL=
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/slack_bot_token
# NVRX_ATTRSVC_SLACK_NOTIFY_ACTIONS=RESTART,STOP

# -- Build identity ----------------------------------------------------------
# Normally baked at build time and reported by /healthz. Set here only to
# label a rollout the deployment already has a name for.
# NVRX_ATTRSVC_BUILD_TAG=
